From 5fee26699771d1923016cfafab9a10792183b0de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:00:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] sepolicy: revert the removal of ion sepolicy

aosp dropped /dev/ion from platform policy ("Remove ION sepolicy",
9b2d37dc22ca), but legacy vendors on kernels without dma-buf heaps still
allocate through it.  without the label and rules, gralloc and the adreno
driver fail inside every client: surfaceflinger aborts in renderengine,
and apps and bootanimation die in eglInitialize with EGL_NOT_INITIALIZED,
so boot never leaves the oem logo (observed on msm8996 and msm8998 with
lineage 22.2 vendors).

revert it, keeping rw access for the graphics allocator and
surfaceflinger which the adreno blobs need during driver init.
